      "text": "To find out how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we first need to determine her walking rate in miles per minute. We know that Jana takes 24 minutes to walk one mile. Therefore, her walking rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Walking rate} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how far she will walk in 10 minutes. We do this by multiplying her walking rate by the time she spends walking:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\left( \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}} \\right) \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\frac{10}{24} \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nTo express this fraction as a decimal, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{24} = \\frac{10 \\div 2}{24 \\div 2} = \\frac{5}{12}\n\\]\n\nTo convert \\(\\frac{5}{12}\\) to a decimal, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{12} \\approx 0.416667\n\\]\n\nRounding this to the nearest tenth, we get:\n\n\\[\n0.416667 \\approx 0.4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance Jana will walk in 10 minutes is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.4}\n\\]",
